From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 04:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: route LINEOUT to the speaker

With 0082 the H616 codec driver binds and registers an ALSA card, and mpv opens
the PCM and writes audio -- but nothing is heard, and /sys/kernel/debug/gpio
shows the amp enable still low during playback:

  gpio-2   (                    |allwinner,pa        ) out lo

sun4i-codec's H616 card provides SND_SOC_DAPM_SPK("Speaker",
sun4i_codec_spk_event), and that event handler is what drives the PA GPIO. Its
built-in routes end at LINEOUT and nothing reaches Speaker, so with
card->fully_routed set DAPM powers the output path down and the event never
fires.

Supplying the board half of the routing connects them. This is why the driver
only warns rather than fails when allwinner,audio-routing is missing -- the
property is board-specific by design. The warning at probe was not cosmetic,
which is worth stating because it was initially read that way.

With this route, gpio-2 reads "out hi" during playback and returns low after
the stream closes. The H713 headphone-amplifier stage required for normal
speaker gain is enabled by the following codec patch.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -776,6 +776,20 @@
 			dma-names = "tx";
 			/* PL2 on r_pio, NOT PB2 on the main pio. Active high. */
 			allwinner,pa-gpios = <&r_pio 0 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			/*
+			 * Without this the amp never turns on. The card carries
+			 * a "Speaker" widget whose event handler toggles the PA
+			 * GPIO above, but its built-in routes stop at LINEOUT
+			 * and nothing reaches Speaker. The card is fully_routed,
+			 * so DAPM powers down the whole output path and the
+			 * event never fires -- measured: playback opened the
+			 * PCM and wrote audio while gpio-2 stayed "out lo".
+			 *
+			 * This is the board-specific half of the routing, which
+			 * is why the driver only warns when it is absent rather
+			 * than failing. The warning is not cosmetic.
+			 */
+			allwinner,audio-routing = "Speaker", "LINEOUT";
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
